OPAL 3.12.10: give the generated revision header a revision

make/toplevel.mak generates revision.h from revision.h.in by extracting a number
out of the file's Subversion $Revision$ keyword.  These sources are consumed from
a git mirror, where that keyword is never expanded, so the extraction yields
nothing and the generated header reads `#define SVN_REVISION` with no value -
which makes OpalGetVersion() in src/opal/manager.cxx a syntax error.

Seeding the keyword with 0 makes the generated header read
`#define SVN_REVISION 0`, which is what the retained source tree that produced
this project's installed OPAL carried.  0 rather than an invented number: the
value only reaches OpalGetVersion()'s "(svn:%u)" suffix, and a git mirror has no
Subversion revision to report honestly.  This is the same repair the pinned
PTLib needs, for the same reason, in its own copy of the same mechanism.

Applies to: a9091f39fcb16f66da2b1134646f341a741a1d15 (branch v3_12)
Upstream:   https://git.code.sf.net/p/opalvoip/opal

diff --git a/revision.h.in b/revision.h.in
index f6e13d0..2b06df8 100644
--- a/revision.h.in
+++ b/revision.h.in
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
  *
  * Contributor(s): ______________________________________.
  *
- * $Revision$
+ * $Revision: 0 $
  * $Author$
  * $Date$
  */
